# Vue `<script setup>` Organization

Order the top-level bindings in `<script setup>` into these sections, declaring each only when the component needs it. Respect dependency order (e.g. a ref feeding a query is declared before the query).

1. Types (interfaces/type aliases)
2. Constants (module-level, `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`)
3. Props (`defineProps`) and emits (`defineEmits`)
4. Composables and stores
5. Reactive state (`ref`/`reactive`)
6. Data fetching (queries) and mutations
7. Computed
8. Form validation
9. Watchers
10. Methods (grouped by concern)
11. Lifecycle hooks

Label each present section with a banner comment sized to its label:

```
// +----------------+
// | Reactive state |
// +----------------+
```

Do not scatter declarations by ad-hoc proximity or place a lifecycle hook before the state it resets. Do co-locate a declaration with the section it belongs to, moving it earlier only when a later binding depends on it.
